This is due to the way we process modules.  We expect to do so in an RPO (parents before children, anyway) manner, since we modify modules when visiting (if inlining into); it's required for correctness of our datastructures and how we use them.

Consider:
``` mlir
firrtl.circuit "Parent" {
  hw.hierpath private @nla [@Grandchild::@ggc_sym, @GreatGrandchild::@target]

